{"additions":4,"author":{"id":"U_kgDODD-3Zw","is_bot":false,"login":"ainyan03","name":"AI nyan"},"baseRefName":"develop","body":"Two commits.\n\n### 1. PaperDIY: no external I2C (Ex_I2C) pins\n\nPaperDIY has no Grove port. G42 / G41 (SYS_SCL / SYS_SDA) are the internal I2C bus and reach only the FPC-I2S expansion connector ([official PinMap](https://docs.m5stack.com/en/core/PaperDIY_Complete_Kit)), so `Ex_I2C` was the same bus as `In_I2C`. The pin table now has no external I2C pins for PaperDIY, matching the M5GFX board catalog (m5stack/M5GFX#447; **please merge the two together**).\n\n**Behavior change on PaperDIY:**\n\n- The internal I2C keeps its pins but moves from port 0 to port 1 (on Arduino, `Wire1` instead of `Wire`), as on PaperS3. `Wire` is left free for the sketch. A sketch that opens `Wire` on G41 / G42 itself now competes with the internal bus (PMIC); use `M5.In_I2C` for devices on the FPC-I2S pins 4 / 5.\n- `Ex_I2C` has no port: `M5.getPin(port_a_*)` returns -1, and `cfg.external_rtc` / `cfg.external_imu` and the Unit display autodetection do not look for devices, as on other boards without a Grove port.\n\n### 2. Do not begin Ex_I2C on boards without external I2C pins\n\nOn a board whose pin table has no external I2C pins, `Ex_I2C` keeps port -1. With `cfg.external_rtc` or `cfg.external_imu` set, `M5.begin()` still called `Ex_I2C.begin()`, and M5GFX opens port -1 as a software I2C port on the pins that port last used. After board detection those are the internal I2C pins, so their GPIO routing was reset. `begin()` is now called only when `Ex_I2C` has a port. This applies to every board without a Grove port, not only PaperDIY.\n\n### Checks\n\n- On a PaperDIY: `M5.begin()` detects the board and the display works.\n- Built for the CI targets (Arduino and ESP-IDF versions); no new warnings.\n- Fork CI passed.\n","changedFiles":1,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-25T11:32:17Z","deletions":2,"files":[{"path":"src/M5Unified.inl","additions":4,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"headRefName":"paperdiy_no_ex_i2c","headRefOid":"bf06bc4ef325a2776d23348c08f3bb6976a59e5c","mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":451,"reviews":[],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-25T11:34:46Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/m5stack/M5Unified/actions/runs/45605371515/job/139174750057","name":"esp32:esp32:esp32 (3.0.7)","startedAt":"2026-11-25T11:33:30Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Arduino Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-25T11:36:47Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/m5stack/M5Unified/actions/runs/45605371459/job/139174751024","name":"esp32 (IDF 5.2.6)","startedAt":"2026-11-25T11:34:48Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"ESP-IDF Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-25T11:33:34Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/m5stack/M5Unified/actions/runs/45605371529/job/139174755004","name":"forward","startedAt":"2026-11-25T11:33:27Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Forward events to WeCom digest"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-25T11:33:54Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/m5stack/M5Unified/actions/runs/45605371586/job/139174749509","name":"single translation unit consistency","startedAt":"2026-11-25T11:33:50Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"SourceCheck"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-25T11:38:43Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/m5stack/M5Unified/actions/runs/45605371515/job/139174750814","name":"esp32:esp32:esp32s3 (3.0.7)","startedAt":"2026-11-25T11:37:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Arduino Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-25T11:38:47Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/m5stack/M5Unified/actions/runs/45605371459/job/139174751054","name":"esp32 (IDF 5.3)","startedAt":"2026-11-25T11:36:36Z","status":"COMPLETED